Subject: Re: Bug on position=dodge?
Message-ID: <FZdtUabnpik.RU1qwAiqEd0J@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <FZdtUabnpik.8v5jF_yW24AJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
References: <FZdtUabnpik.8v5jF_yW24AJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/FZdtUabnpik/m/RU1qwAiqEd0J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

It is a bug.  You can see it with an even simpler example:

df1 <- data.frame(x=1, y=1)
ggplot(df1, aes(x=x, y=y)) + geom_point(position="dodge")

I've filed a bug report (and proposed patch): https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/issues/issue/157

--
Brian S. Diggs, PhD
Senior Research Associate, Department of Surgery
Oregon Health & Science University

