if you want to go the discrete route, you'll have to do something like cut() on z (see below)  and also fiddle with scale_fill_manual. this is nearly the same as what brandon did with _gradientn

 conc20<-melt(mat_conc20)
 names(conc20) <- c("y", "x", "z")

## *** ##
conc20$z=cut(conc20$z,6,include.lowest=TRUE)

conc20_cont <- ggplot(conc20, aes(x, y, z = z))

conc20_cont + geom_tile(aes(fill=z)) + scale_fill_manual(values=c("blue","lightblue","green","yellow","orange","red"))

