yes, I worked out this with all your valuable help
(it's working with brandon's definition of variable names, different
from my original one and luciano's)

ggplot(data, aes(x.avg, y.avg))+
geom_point(size=2, colour="blue")+
geom_errorbar(aes(ymin=y.avg-y.lower, ymax=y.avg+y.upper), size=0.1,
colour="red")+
geom_errorbarh(aes(xmin=x.avg-x.lower, xmax=x.avg+x.upper), size=0.1,
colour="red")+
geom_text(aes(label=labels, x = x.label, y = y.label), size=3,
hjust=0)+
geom_segment(aes(xend = x.label, yend = y.label), linetype = "dashed")
+

geom_abline(intercept = 0, slope = 1)+
scale_y_log10()+
scale_x_log10()

still something to sort out: is there a way to automatically place
labels in a good position so that they do not overlap?
It is just to generalise the script for other data sets I might be
using...
Is it possible to complete the type of the wiskers with a short
perpendicular line, like in the example I posted here
https://sites.google.com/site/wantedchart/

thanks for all your time, I'm learning a deal in such a short time
this blessed forum is really great

max

